title: Spread the Strike
subtitle: Berlin is out. The rest of Germany is wavering.
view-if: crisis_cuno = 1
on-arrival: month_actions += 1
frequency: 100
is-card: true
new-page: true
tags: crisis

= Spread the Strike

The strike is strongest in Berlin and weakest where the unions are strongest. Hamburg's docks are out; its shipyards are not. The Ruhr miners are already on strike against the French. The railwaymen have not moved since their own defeat last year.

- @railways: Send our best speakers to the railway depots.
- @provinces: Send couriers to every district with the strike call.
- @ruhr: Bring the Ruhr pit committees into the strike.

@railways
subtitle: If the trains stop, the strike becomes national. A long shot.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.worker_support >= 30) {
    Q.crisis_momentum += 9;
    Q.e23_rail_joined = 1;
} else {
    Q.crisis_momentum += 3;
    Q.e23_rail_joined = 0;
}
Q.repression += 2;
!}

[? if e23_rail_joined = 1 : The Berlin and Leipzig depots vote to come out. By evening the trains stop on the main lines. ?][? if e23_rail_joined = 0 : The railwaymen listen politely and go back to their engines. A few depots stop work for a day. ?]

@provinces
subtitle: Costs 1 fund. The strike spreads more evenly.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no funds for couriers.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; crisis_momentum += 6; worker_support += 2

Couriers on motorcycles carry the strike call to Stettin, Breslau and Königsberg. The provincial towns come out a day late, but they come out.

@ruhr
subtitle: The Ruhr Left is eager. The French may take advantage.
on-arrival: crisis_momentum += 5; district_ruhr_loyalty += 4; militancy += 3

The Ruhr pit committees turn their strike against the French into a strike against Cuno. The occupation authorities watch the Germans fight each other with interest.
